-- coa2-ch5-ch6-name-change-disclosure.l4: Part 5, Chapter 5 (Change of name) and Chapter 6 (Trading disclosures), ss 77-85,
-- lines 983-1054 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 283 "special resolution" (coa7), s 1033 "company's name on restoration to the register" (coa22).
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Chapter 5: Change of name (ss 77-81)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 77(1) way of changing the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 77(1)(a) by special resolution`
    `s 77(1)(b) by other means provided for by the company's articles`

-- src:984 | 77 Change of name
-- src:985 | (1) A company may change its name—
-- src:986 | (a) by special resolution (see section 78), or
-- src:987 | (b) by other means provided for by the company's articles (see section 79).
@ref s 77(1) A company may change its name (src:984-987)
GIVEN way IS A `s 77(1) way of changing the name`
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for the other means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(1) the company may change its name in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 77(1)(a) by special resolution` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by special resolution (see section 78)"; whether the resolution is a special resolution is s 283's answer
    WHEN `s 77(1)(b) by other means provided for by the company's articles` THEN
        IF `the articles provide for the other means`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by other means provided for by the company's articles (see section 79)"

DECLARE `s 77(2) way of changing the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 77(2)(a) by resolution of the directors acting under section 64`
    `s 77(2)(b) on the determination of a new name by a company names adjudicator under section 73`
    `s 77(2)(c) on the determination of a new name by the court under section 74`
    `s 77(2)(d) under section 1033 (company's name on restoration to the register)`
    `s 77(2)(e) by resolution of the directors acting under section 45(3) of the Charities Act 2011`

-- src:984 | 77 Change of name
-- src:988 | (2) The name of a company may also be changed—
-- src:989 | (a) by resolution of the directors acting under section 64 (change of name to comply with direction of Secretary of State under that section);
-- src:990 | (b) on the determination of a new name by a company names adjudicator under section 73 (powers of adjudicator on upholding objection to company name);
-- src:991 | (c) on the determination of a new name by the court under section 74 (appeal against decision of company names adjudicator);
-- src:992 | (d) under section 1033 (company's name on restoration to the register).
-- src:993 | (e) by resolution of the directors acting under section 45(3) of the Charities Act 2011 (change of name to comply with direction of Charity Commission).
@ref s 77(2) The name may also be changed (src:984-993)
GIVEN way IS A `s 77(2) way of changing the name`
      `the change is made in the circumstances that paragraph describes (for (d), s 1033 the company's name is changed on restoration to the register)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(2) the name of the company may also be changed in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the change is made in the circumstances that paragraph describes (for (d), s 1033 the company's name is changed on restoration to the register)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The name of a company may also be changed— (a) ... (e)", each in the circumstances the paragraph names

-- src:994 | 78 Change of name by special resolution
-- src:995 | (1) Where a change of name has been agreed to by a company by special resolution, the company must give notice to the registrar.
-- src:996 | This is in addition to the obligation to forward a copy of the resolution to the registrar.
@ref s 78(1) Notice to the registrar of a change of name by special resolution (src:994-996)
GIVEN `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a change of name has been agreed to by the company by that resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a change of name has been agreed to by the company by that resolution`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a change of name has been agreed to by a company by special resolution, the company must give notice to the registrar."
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a change of name has been agreed to by a company by special resolution"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is a special resolution is s 283's answer and it is not known

-- src:994 | 78 Change of name by special resolution
-- src:997 | (2) Where a change of name by special resolution is conditional on the occurrence of an event, the notice given to the registrar of the change must—
-- src:998 | (a) specify that the change is conditional, and
