GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(3)(a) the registrar is not required to act under section 80 until further notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice states that the event has not occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the notice states that the event has not occurred— (a) the registrar is not required to act under section 80 (registration and issue of new certificate of incorporation) until further notice"

-- src:1000 | (3) If the notice states that the event has not occurred—
-- src:1002 | (b) when the event occurs, the company must give notice to the registrar stating that it has occurred, and
@ref s 78(3)(b) The company must give notice when the event occurs (src:1000-1002)
