-- src:1000 | (3) If the notice states that the event has not occurred—
-- src:1003 | (c) the registrar may rely on the statement as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it.
@ref s 78(3)(c) The registrar may rely on the statement (src:1000-1003)
GIVEN `the company has given notice to the registrar stating that the event has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(3)(c) the registrar may rely on the statement as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it` MEANS
    IF `the company has given notice to the registrar stating that the event has occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the registrar may rely on the statement"; there is no statement to rely on

