-- src:1009 | 80 Change of name: registration and issue of new certificate of incorporation
-- src:1010 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:1011 | (a) the registrar receives notice of a change of a company’s name and is satisfied—
-- src:1012 | (i) that the new name complies with the requirements of this Part, and
-- src:1013 | (ii) that the requirements of the Companies Acts, and any relevant requirements of the company’s articles, with respect to a change of name are complied with, or
-- src:1014 | (b) the registrar determines a new name for a company under section 76C or 76D.
@ref s 80(1) Registration and issue of new certificate: when the section applies (src:1009-1014)
GIVEN `the registrar receives notice of a change of the company's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that the new name complies with the requirements of Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that the requirements of the Companies Acts, and any relevant requirements of the company's articles, with respect to a change of name are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar determines a new name for the company under section 76C or 76D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF       (    `the registrar receives notice of a change of the company's name`
              AND `the registrar is satisfied that the new name complies with the requirements of Part 5`
              AND `the registrar is satisfied that the requirements of the Companies Acts, and any relevant requirements of the company's articles, with respect to a change of name are complied with`)
         OR  `the registrar determines a new name for the company under section 76C or 76D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:1015 | (2) The registrar must enter the new name on the register in place of the former name.
@ref s 80(2) The registrar must enter the new name on the register (src:1015-1015)
GIVEN `the section applies (s 80(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(2) the registrar must enter the new name on the register in place of the former name` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies (s 80(1))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where—"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

-- src:1016 | (3) On the registration of the new name, the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 80(3) The registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances (src:1016-1016)
