    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the registration of the new name, the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case"

-- src:1017 | 81 Change of name: effect
-- src:1018 | (1) A change of a company's name has effect from the date on which the new certificate of incorporation is issued.
@ref s 81(1) Change of name: the change has effect from the date of the new certificate (src:1017-1018)
GIVEN `the date on which the new certificate of incorporation is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) the change of name has effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the new certificate of incorporation is issued`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A change of a company's name has effect from the date on which the new certificate of incorporation is issued" (no certificate has been issued, so the change has no effect yet)
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF day AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has effect from the date on which the new certificate of incorporation is issued"

-- src:1019 | (2) The change does not affect any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against it.
@ref s 81(2) The change does not affect rights or obligations or proceedings (src:1019-1019)
GIVEN `it is a right or obligation of the company, or legal proceedings by or against it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(2) the change of name affects the right, the obligation or the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `it is a right or obligation of the company, or legal proceedings by or against it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The change does not affect any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against it."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of the company's rights and obligations and of legal proceedings by or against it

