-- src:1033 | 83 Civil consequences of failure to make required disclosure
-- src:1034 | (1) This section applies to any legal proceedings brought by a company to which section 82 applies (requirement to disclose company name etc) to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business in respect of which the company was, at the time the contract was made, in breach of regulations under that section.
@ref s 83(1) Civil consequences of failure to make required disclosure: when the section applies (src:1033-1034)
GIVEN `the proceedings are legal proceedings brought by a company to which section 82 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are brought to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was, at the time the contract was made, in breach of regulations under section 82 in respect of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(1) this section applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF       `the proceedings are legal proceedings brought by a company to which section 82 applies`
         AND `the proceedings are brought to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business`
         AND `the company was, at the time the contract was made, in breach of regulations under section 82 in respect of that business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to any legal proceedings brought by a company ... to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business in respect of which the company was, at the time the contract was made, in breach of regulations under that section"

-- src:1035 | (2) The proceedings shall be dismissed if the defendant (in Scotland, the defender) to the proceedings shows—
-- src:1036 | (a) that he has a claim against the claimant (pursuer) arising out of the contract that he has been unable to pursue by reason of the latter's breach of the regulations, or
-- src:1037 | (b) that he has suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's (pursuer's) breach of the regulations,
-- src:1038 | unless the court before which the proceedings are brought is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue.
@ref s 83(2) The proceedings shall be dismissed (src:1035-1038)
GIVEN `the section applies to the proceedings (s 83(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the defendant shows that he has a claim against the claimant arising out of the contract that he has been unable to pursue by reason of the claimant's breach of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant shows that he has suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's breach of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies to the proceedings (s 83(1))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `the defendant shows that he has a claim against the claimant arising out of the contract that he has been unable to pursue by reason of the claimant's breach of the regulations`
             OR  `the defendant shows that he has suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's breach of the regulations`
        THEN IF `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court before which the proceedings are brought is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The proceedings shall be dismissed if the defendant ... shows— (a) ... or (b) ..."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): this subsection speaks of the proceedings to which the section applies

